<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Africa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> is the western region of the African continent, stretching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-guinea">Gulf of Guinea</a>. It was home to a succession of powerful states, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> empires of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>, the forest kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. Its gold and its role in the trans-Saharan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic trades</a> connected it to the wider world, and it was later colonised largely by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-africa.jpg" alt="West Africa" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hogweard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western-Africa-map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
